  "data_abstract": "The first measurements of light antinucleus production in Au+Au collisions at the Relativistic Heavy-Ion Collider are reported. The observed production rates for $\\overline{d}$ and $^3\\overline{\\mathrm{He}}$ are much larger than in lower energy nucleus-nucleus collisions. A coalescence model analysis of the yields indicates that there is little or no increase in the antinucleon freeze-out volume compared to collisions at CERN SPS energy. These analyses also indicate that the $^3\\overline{\\mathrm{He}}$ freeze-out volume is smaller than the $\\overline{d}$ freeze-out volume.",
